<title>SOUTH KOREA: POSCO says buys 1,000T of ferro-chrome.</title>
<headline>POSCO says buys 1,000T of ferro-chrome.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pohang Iron and Steel Co Ltd (POSCO) bought 1,000 tonnes of ferro-chrome through a tender on January 17, a POSCO official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The second best offer was made by Enerco Ag at 74.5 cent/lb, C&amp;F. The official declined to give price details for the winner.</p>
<p>The chemical specification of the ferro-chrome include chrome at minimum 53 percent, carbon at maximum 3.0 percent, silicon at maximum 0.5 percent, and sulphur and phosphorus at maximum 0.025 percent, the official said.</p>
<p>Shipment was set during February to the port city of Pusan.</p>
<p>POSCO is the largest steel maker in South Korea.  </p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
